## Getting started

`dude` is the project CLI. It ships as a **private package** on GitHub Packages,
so first authenticate the registry, then install the global launcher, then
provision and start the app.

```bash
# 1. One-time machine setup — authenticate the private @cubocicloide registry.
#    Add to ~/.npmrc:
#      @cubocicloide:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
#      //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
#    …and export a GitHub token with the `read:packages` scope:
export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your_token_here

# 2. Install the dude launcher globally (the only global install).
npm install -g @cubocicloide/dude-launcher

# 3. Scaffold the project (how {{projectName}} was created). Already inside it
#    or cloned it? Skip this and go straight to `pnpm install`.
dude init {{projectName}}
cd {{projectName}}

# 4. Provision the project's pinned toolchain (CLI + stack) from the lockfile.
pnpm install

# 5. Start everything. The FIRST boot provisions the bench and the site
#    (downloads Frappe{{#if withHelpdesk}}, installs Helpdesk{{/if}}, installs the custom apps) —
#    this takes several minutes. Watch the progress:
dude up
dude logs --service bench
```

From then on, `dude up` starts everything and `dude down` stops it (the bench
and database persist in Docker volumes; `dude down --volumes` wipes them). See
[Working with dude](dude.md) for the full command reference.

To serve this documentation site:

```bash
dude docs          # → http://localhost:8001
```

